{
  "openapi": "3.0.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "UTM IO API",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "description": "The UTM.io API is rate limited per account across one-minute and one-day windows, each counted from your first request in that window. Every authenticated response tells you where your account stands in each window: `X-RateLimit-Limit-Minute`, `X-RateLimit-Remaining-Minute` and `X-RateLimit-Reset-Minute` (seconds until that window rolls over), and the same three headers for `-Day`. Read those rather than assuming a figure — your allowance depends on your plan. Contact support if you need it raised. Exceeding either window returns a `429 Too Many Requests` response with a `Retry-After` header giving the number of seconds to wait before retrying; that response carries the rate-limit headers for both windows too, so you can tell a one-minute burst from an exhausted daily allowance."
  },
